An indented code block after the line that closed a list or blockquote is one block

A flag that limits an indented code block to one line was set whenever a line closed a list item or
blockquote, and stayed set until the next indented code block read it. When the closing line held
another block (a thematic break, a heading, a fence), the next code block, lines later, was cut
after its first line, so `- a\n\n\n***\n    code\n\n    more\n` parsed as two code blocks. The rule
it copies from micromark applies only to code that starts on the closing line itself, so the line
now works that out for itself and the flag is gone.

